A46 — composite through a storage shadow when the scan-out modifier cannot be a storage image

gamescope writes its composite straight into the flippable scan-out image,
so the DRM backend only accepts a primary-plane format whose DRM modifier
offers sampled, storage and transfer-src support. The PowerVR driver on the
Pixel 10 (24.3) offers no such modifier for any of XRGB2101010, XBGR2101010
or XRGB8888 with the LINEAR modifier the gamenative-drm daemon scans out,
so drm_initialize failed with "Primary plane doesn't support any formats
>= 8888" and gamescope died.

When the first pick finds nothing, the backend logs each plane format's
optimal, linear and per-modifier tiling features, picks again asking only
for transfer-dst from the modifier but storage, sampled and transfer-src
from the format's optimal tiling (the PowerVR driver has storage only on
RGBA8, never on BGRA8, so the pick lands on XBGR8888; XBGR8888/ABGR8888 is
the last pair tried for the primary and overlay planes), and sets
g_bOutputStorageShadow. The output images are
then created as plain copy destinations and each gets an optimal-tiled
shadow with the storage, sampled and transfer-src usage; vulkan_composite
targets the shadow and copies it into the scan-out image on the same
command buffer, so the present-layout and foreign-queue barriers on the
scan-out image stay as they were. Drivers where the first pick succeeds
take the old path unchanged.

